67 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 285 0 R
/T (Problem Statement Title- Modern healthcare is broken because patients don't own their medical data. Records are trapped in centralized hospital databases that are vulnerable to ransomware and fracture every time a patient switches providers. This forces reliance on easily lost paper documents and offers no secure way to transfer health record ownership from a parent to a child when they turn 18. As a result, individuals lack a portable, lifelong health identity and have zero control over their own life-saving medical information.)
/E (Problem Statement Title- Modern healthcare is broken because patients don't own their medical data. Records are trapped in centralized hospital databases that are vulnerable to ransomware and fracture every time a patient switches providers. This forces reliance on easily lost paper documents and offers no secure way to transfer health record ownership from a parent to a child when they turn 18. As a result, individuals lack a portable, lifelong health identity and have zero control over their own life-saving medical information.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
